        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T04:46:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I debated this a bit, and I lament that the charger API for the chip\ndoesn\u0027t have the right methods. It\u0027s somewhat complicated by the fact that this only is used for the primary charger, requiring some special case.\nPlumbing it into the chip\u0027s tcpc driver seemed.. hmmm... ugly and cuts across\nthe driver boundaries (separate charger and TCPC drivers).\nThere didn\u0027t appear to be convenient places to hook it onto anything in driver/tcpm/raa489000.c\n\nIs it just the fact it is polled that is the issue? It\u0027s likely not that much overhead (reading and checking one register).\n\nI would have liked it to have been hooked into one of the charger API calls, but I am not sure which (if any) are suitable - none were obvious. There are some that are called regularly by the charger code (e.g get_status etc.) but it didn\u0027t seem good to rely on that.\n\nKeeping it entirely in the charger driver seemed to be better functional separation, at the cost of it being polled (because of the lack of a good hook somewhere).",
      "parentUuid": "7fa42f7c_b58aeb3f",
      "revId": "88e2368a06d89c793c881ffa036998f742952872",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "34625588_76d96743",
        "filename": "driver/charger/isl923x.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1491,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T04:57:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it\u0027s mostly that polling feels like a messy way to achieve this even if the cost is pretty small (although I\u0027m not sure how small it really is, since this will probably consume on the order of 100 microseconds of CPU time per second, forever including while in sleep and there are only a small number of HOOK_SECOND users: one more could be a significant change to EC power draw under AP-off conditions).\n\nI agree that there\u0027s nowhere good to put it in either the TCPM or charger driver as things stand, since mode changes can happen semi-autonomously (thinking of FRS in particular) and there won\u0027t be any callbacks to change the charger mode. The type-C state machine will always be updated to remain in sync though, so I think adding some kind of hook in there is quite reasonable.",
      "parentUuid": "87eceeea_13d933be",
      "revId": "88e2368a06d89c793c881ffa036998f742952872",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
